From 5dcfc0eca76c9df98ec1da7ef95b6b48523206ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skippy contributors <ci@skippy.local>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:57:08 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] llama: run a prompt chunk and the decodes of other sequences
 in one ubatch

A hybrid model's memory splits a batch with split_equal, which takes the
same number of tokens from every sequence. A batch with a prompt chunk
for one sequence and one decode token for each of the others became two
ubatches: one token of every sequence, then the rest of the prompt. Each
ubatch is a full pass over the weights, so a mixed step cost about two
steps, and the decodes waited for the prompt.

split_equal_grouped takes from every sequence set up to one level, the
most that fits n_ubatch, so short sets fit whole and the long one takes
the rest. The sets form up to four groups of equal length. A grouped
ubatch lists the tokens and the unique seq ids group by group, and gives
each group a view that shares its arrays at the group's offset.

The models that opt in (qwen35, qwen35moe) run the projections and the
attention output once over all the tokens. Per group, they run the conv
and gated delta net on views of the projections and of the states, which
build_rs reads once, and write the states of the group's cells. With
kv_rows, attention runs per group too, over the cell lists of the group's
view, so a decode does not read the cells of the prompt's sequence.

An equal ubatch is one group, and builds the same graph as before.
Grouped graphs are not reused. LLAMA_GROUPED_UBATCH_DISABLE keeps the
equal splits, to measure against them.
